# QuoteIQ — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT VALUES ONLY.
#
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored):    cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Laid out to match a Doppler env export (alphabetical, KEY="value") so the two example files read
# the same way — but nothing here comes from Doppler. Every value below belongs to the Supabase
# stack running on your own machine via Docker. Print the current ones at any time with:
#
#     npx supabase status
#
# The local anon and service-role keys are the well-known fixed keys the Supabase CLI prints for
# every local project. They are LOCAL-ONLY: they are not secrets, they grant nothing beyond your
# machine, and they must never be copied into a deployed environment's configuration. Deployed
# values are cataloged in .env.example and docs/environment-variables.md, and live in Doppler.
#
# The keys are stable across `supabase start` and `db reset`, so you normally paste them once.

# Any non-empty string works locally. Minimum 16 characters.
API_KEY_PEPPER="<local-only-api-key-pepper-min-16-chars>"

# Any non-empty strings work locally; deployed environments must use generated high-entropy values.
CRON_SECRET="<local-only-cron-secret>"
INTERNAL_JOB_SECRET="<local-only-job-secret>"

# The server reads its own SUPABASE_URL/SUPABASE_ANON_KEY (Supabase Auth token verification)
# rather than the VITE_-prefixed browser values below.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="<local-anon-key-from-supabase-status>"

# The local stack's connection pooler is disabled by default ([db.pooler] in supabase/config.toml),
# so BOTH point at the direct 54322 port. Deployed environments split them: the pooler (6543) for
# runtime traffic, the direct connection (5432) for migrations and admin work.
#
# Substitute <local-db-password> with the local stack's password, which is `postgres` (printed in
# full by `npx supabase status` as DB_URL). It is a placeholder here because this repository
# forbids any committed example file from containing an inline connection-string password, local
# or not — src/server/tests/integration/env-examples.test.ts enforces that.
SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:<local-db-password>@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres"
SUPABASE_DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:<local-db-password>@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres"

# Bypasses RLS and drives the Auth Admin API (user provisioning, T-017).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="<local-service-role-key-from-supabase-status>"
SUPABASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:54321"

# Browser-safe: exposed to the SPA through Vite import.meta.env.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="<local-anon-key-from-supabase-status>"
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:54321"

# --- Optional server settings (defaults shown; assign only to override) ---
# APP_ENV defaults to `local`, which is correct here and is what permits STORAGE_ADAPTER="fake".
#   Deployed environments MUST set it — see .env.example.
# JOB_CRON_BASE_URL                            unset here on purpose. It is the DEPLOYED origin the
#   pg_cron schedules call back on, read only by `npm run db:cron:configure`. Local development has
#   no such origin — the schedules are documented no-ops locally (Q-7) — so leave it alone unless
#   you are deliberately pointing a local database at a reachable server.
# LOG_LEVEL="<debug|info|warn|error>"          defaults to `info`; `debug` helps on request/job logging
# NODE_ENV="<development|production|test>"     defaults to `development`
# STORAGE_ADAPTER="<supabase|fake>"            defaults to `supabase`; `fake` is the in-memory test
#   seam, permitted only in a local environment (composition refuses it in dev/preview/staging/production).
# STORAGE_ATTACHMENTS_BUCKET="<bucket-name>"   defaults to `quote-attachments` (the private bucket from migrations)
